<!-- The A11 (177525642#1 eastbound, 286750932#2 westbound) now ends at the new junction and goes on as new edges a11_*:
     a third lane for 150-230 m before each exit and after each entry, as netconvert's ramp guessing gave the other exits.
     Ramps at 40 km/h, as at Lucca Est: direct ramps from and to Florence along the north side; from Pisa a loop south of the
     motorway and a flyover; to Pisa a hook onto the north side, east of the Via di Sorbano del Vescovo overpass. The exit
     road (two lanes each way; the toll plaza is its 40 km/h stretch, toll booths are not simulated, as at the other exits)
     leads to R1, the study's 40 m roundabout on Via di Mugnano at Via Dario Vitali (two-lane ring); R2 is the study's
     roundabout at Via Giovanni Diodati (one-lane ring). R0 replaces the 18 m mini-roundabout at Via di Mugnano / Via Enrico
     Squaglia / Via Enrico Mattei, where the exit's traffic meets the roads to the city, with a 40 m two-lane ring: an
     addition to the study, whose design stops at R2. The roads linking them and Via Giovanni Diodati, the study's route for
     lorries, are upgraded to tertiary roads; Via di Mugnano through the village east of R2 is calmed to 30 km/h (the
     compensation measures in QC.Sa.2). -->
